\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Weak locality in the scalar CTP comparison}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{\citet{§§1–2, pp. 409–412, especially Sätze 1–2}{jost1957ctp}
assumes covariance of vacuum correlation functions under
translations and the connected proper orthochronous Lorentz
group, a positive-energy spectrum and a unique vacuum at zero
energy-momentum.
The spectrum and covariance give the analytic continuation
to the extended tube used in his scalar argument.
The weak locality condition reverses the order of the
vacuum correlations on the specified real spacelike
configurations. Satz 1 requires the reversal at real Jost
points. Satz 2 assumes it in a real neighborhood of such a
point and gives the CTP relation at arbitrary real arguments.
This continuum CPT result, titled CTP in the source, is
cited, not proved here.}

\p{The finite total inversion of \ref{fdip-019E} instead
uses an even number of antiunitary field maps and a finite
coordinate pullback. Its determinant equality comes from
the unitary conjugation of \ref{fdip-019F}, on spin fields
with their prescribed finite link transports.}
